  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Phil reports:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I have found a bug in all the 3.1 client shell scripts.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "e.g. fedora-find.sh synopsis at:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/FCR30/Client+Command-line+Utilities"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/FCR30/Client+Command-line+Utilities",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "suggests (with ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-86#icft=FCREPO-86"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": " applied) this example should work:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "fedora-find localhost 8080 userid password \"pid fType title description\" \"fedora\" http",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It does not work because the code (with ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-86#icft=FCREPO-86"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": " applied) says:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "(exec $JAVA_HOME/bin/java ... $1 $2 $3 $4 $5 $6 $7)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The exec means that the fieldList ($5) gets expanded as follows",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "before execution (which is wrong – it should not be expanded, but",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "rather be seen by the shell as a single argument):",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "pid fType title description",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It also means that wild carding with \"?\" and \"*\" for the search string",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "($6) will match files in the current working directory instead of being",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "passed through to the java application.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The fix is to quote all the shell arguments, thus:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "(exec $JAVA_HOME/bin/java ... \"$1\" \"$2\" \"$3\" \"$4\" \"$5\" \"$6\" \"$7\")",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I expect that this bug is present in all the shell scripts.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
  "duedate": null,
  "environment": null,
